{
	"_comment": [
		"Source of truth for NBR dashboard pages. The scraper never hardcodes URLs or filter labels in Python.",
		"A filter is either a plain label string (read-only: the scraper records whatever value the dashboard shows)",
		"or an object: {\"label\": ..., \"options\": [...]} to iterate every option, or {\"label\": ..., \"fixed\": \"All\"} to force one value.",
		"If a page has no \"filters\" key, its filter list is UNVERIFIED: the scraper records the labels/values it actually finds",
		"and warns. Run `--discover --page <id>` to list the real labels/options, then paste them here.",
		"known_not_applicable / known_no_data: lists of partial filter matches that are recorded without scraping."
	],
	"defaults": {
		"gender_distribution": true,
		"date_selector": "#date"
	},
	"pages": {
		"cards": {
			"title": "Cards",
			"url": "https://fininclusion.bnr.rw/touchpoints/cards",
